urce` |\\n   414\\t| Detach source | DELETE | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments/:sourceAttachmentId` | `detachSource` |\\n   415\\t| Get process source provenance | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-provenance` | `listProcessSourceProvenance` |\\n   416\\t\\n   417\\tAll routes require authenticated access. Project-scoped routes call the existing\\n   418\\t`app.projectAccessService`; process-scoped attach/provenance reads also call\\n   419\\t`app.processAccessService`.\\n   420\\t\\n   421\\t### Error Codes\\n   422\\t\\n   423\\t| Status | Code | Meaning |\\n   424\\t|--------|------|---------|\\n   425\\t| 401 | `UNAUTHENTICATED` | Actor is missing |\\n   426\\t| 403 | `PROJECT_FORBIDDEN` | Actor lacks project access |\\n   427\\t| 403 | `PROCESS_FORBIDDEN` | Actor lacks process access |\\n   428\\t| 404 | `PROJECT_NOT_FOUND` | Project does not exist |\\n   429\\t| 404 | `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` | Process does not exist in project |\\n   430\\t| 404 | `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_NOT_FOUND` | Source attachment does not exist in project |\\n   431\\t| 409 | `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_CONFLICT` | Active row already exists for same identity, scope, and target ref, or the update would violate writable-ref policy |\\n   432\\t| 409 | `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE` | Refresh cannot be accepted for this attachment state |\\n   433\\t| 422 | `INVALID_SOURCE_ATTACHMENT` | Request body, repository identity, or target-ref policy is invalid |\\n   434\\t| 503 | `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_UNAVAILABLE` | GitHub repository/ref cannot be accessed right now |\\n   435\\t\\n   436\\t## Service Interfaces\\n   437\\t\\n   438\\t```typescript\\n   439\\texport interface GitHubRepositoryResolver {\\n   440\\t  resolveRepository(args: {\\n   441\\t    repositoryUrl: string;\\n   442\\t    repositoryFullName?: string;\\n   443\\t    targetRef: string | null;\\n   444\\t  }): Promise<\\n   445\\t    | {\\n   446\\t        kind: 'resolved';\\n   447\\t        repositoryUrl: string;\\n   448\\t        repositoryFullName: string;\\n   449\\t        targetRef: string | null;\\n   450\\t      }\\n   451\\t    | { kind: 'invalid'; message: string }\\n   452\\t    | { kind: 'inaccessible'; message: string }\\n   453\\t  >;\\n   454\\t}\\n   455\\t\\n   456\\texport interface SourceManagementService {\\n   457\\t  attachProjectSource(args: {\\n   458\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\n   459\\t    projectId: string;\\n   460\\t    input: CreateSourceAttachmentRequest;\\n   461\\t  }): Promise<SourceAttachmentSummary>;\\n   462\\t\\n   463\\t  attachProcessSource(args: {\\n   464\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\n   465\\t    projectId: string;\\n   466\\t    processId: string;\\n   467\\t    input: CreateSourceAttachmentRequest;\\n   468\\t  }): Promise<SourceAttachmentSummary>;\\n   469\\t\\n   470\\t  updateSource(args: {\\n   471\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\n   472\\t    projectId: string;\\n   473\\t    sourceAttachmentId: string;\\n   474\\t    input: UpdateSourceAttachmentRequest;\\n   475\\t  }): Promise<SourceAttachmentSummary>;\\n   476\\t\\n   477\\t  detachSource(args: {\\n   478\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\n   479\\t    projectId: string;\\n   480\\t    sourceAttachmentId: string;\\n   481\\t  }): Promise<{ detached: true; sourceAttachmentId: string; detachedAt: string }>;\\n   482\\t}\\n   483\\t\\n   484\\texport interface SourceRefreshService {\\n   485\\t  refreshSource(args: {\\n   486\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\n   487\\t    projectId: string;\\n   488\\t    sourceAttachmentId: string;\\n   489\\t  }): Promise<RefreshSourceAttachmentResponse>;\\n   490\\t}\\n   491\\t\\n   492\\texport interface SourceProvenanceService {\\n   493\\t  recordSourceProvenance(args: {\\n   494\\t    projectId: string;\\n   495\\t    processId: string;\\n   496\\t    sourceAttachmentId: string | null;\\n   497\\t    relationshipKind: SourceProvenanceRelationship;\\n   498\\t    repositoryFullName: string;\\n   499\\t    repositoryUrl: string;\\n   500\\t    targetRef: string | null;\\n   501\\t    eventId?: string | null;\\n   502\\t  }): Promise<SourceProvenanceEntry>;\\n   503\\t\\n   504\\t  listProcessSourceProvenance(args: {\\n   505\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\n   506\\t    projectId: string;\\n   507\\t    processId: string;\\n   508\\t  }): Promise<{ entries: SourceProvenanceEntry[] }>;\\n   509\\t}\\n   510\\t```\\n   511\\t\\n   512\\t## Flow-by-Flow Design\\n   513\\t\\n   514\\t### Flow 1: Attach Repositories\\n   515\\t\\n   516\\tThis flow covers AC-1.1 through AC-1.4. The user attaches a GitHub repository\\n   517\\tfrom either the project shell or a process work surface. Fastify validates scope\\n   518\\tand repository identity before Convex persists the row.\\n   519\\t\\n   520\\t```mermaid\\n   521\\tsequenceDiagram\\n   522\\t    participant U as User\\n   523\\t    participant C as Client Source UI\\n   524\\t    participant R as Fastify Source Route\\n   525\\t    participant S as SourceManagementService\\n   526\\t    participant G as GitHubRepositoryResolver\\n   527\\t    participant P as PlatformStore\\n   528\\t    participant X as Convex\\n   529\\t\\n   530\\t    U->>C: Submit repository URL and metadata\\n   531\\t    C->>R: POST source-attachments\\n   532\\t    Note over R,S: AC-1.1: project or process scoped attach\\n   533\\t    R->>S: attachProjectSource or attachProcessSource\\n   534\\t    S->>G: resolveRepository(url, fullName?, targetRef)\\n   535\\t    Note over S,G: AC-1.4: reject invalid/inaccessible repos\\n   536\\t    G-->>S: canonical repositoryFullName\\n   537\\t    S->>P: createSourceAttachment\\n   538\\t    P->>X: sourceAttachments:createSourceAttachment\\n   539\\t    Note over P,X: AC-1.3: duplicate active row rejected\\n   540\\t    alt Process-scoped attach\\n   541\\t        S->>P: add sourceAttachmentId to current process source refs\\n   542\\t    end\\n   543\\t    X-->>P: persisted row\\n   544\\t    P-->>S: SourceAttachmentSummary\\n   545\\t    S-->>R: summary\\n   546\\t    R-->>C: 201 summary\\n   547\\t```\\n   548\\t\\n   549\\tFor process-scoped attach, `SourceManagementService` must update the process's\\n   550\\tcurrent source refs so the new source appears immediately in\\n   551\\t`materials.currentSources`. Project-scoped attach creates a durable shared\\n   552\\tsource row but does not automatically make that source current for every\\n   553\\tprocess.\\n   554\\t\\n   555\\t### Flow 2: Manage Purpose, Access Mode, and Target Ref\\n   556\\t\\n   557\\tThis flow covers AC-2.1 through AC-2.4. Purpose and access mode are durable\\n   558\\tmetadata. Target ref is part of the source definition; changing it marks a\\n   559\\tpreviously hydrated attachment stale until refresh/rehydration catches up.\\n   560\\t\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/02-manage-purpose-access-mode-and-target-ref/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:294:| `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | unavailable or revoked source reads redact current source details while preserving bounded state | Covers AC-6.2 redaction requirement |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/02-manage-purpose-access-mode-and-target-ref/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:313:invariants, refresh response semantics, unavailable-source redaction, and\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/05-detach-sources-and-preserve-prior-provenance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:288:| `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | unavailable or revoked source reads redact current source details while preserving bounded state | Covers AC-6.2 redaction requirement |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/05-detach-sources-and-pr