9`).\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:585:        evidence: \"`buildUnavailableSourceAttachment` only flips availability-related fields and leaves prior hydration metadata on the summary (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The project-shell reader forwards that summary unchanged (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts`), and the process materials reader still emits `lastHydratedAt` / `freshnessReason` whenever present (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts`). The shared project contract also requires `lastHydratedResolvedRef` and `lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` on every source row (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts`), so unavailable rows returned from real GET surfaces can still expose prior hydration details. The only new TC-6.2a proof is a synthetic UI-envelope test (`tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts`), which means the route/read path required by the story’s anti-shim rule is not actually proving redaction.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:603:        evidence: \"`buildUnavailableSourceAttachment` only flips availability-related fields and leaves prior hydration metadata on the summary (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The project-shell reader forwards that summary unchanged (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts`), and the process materials reader still emits `lastHydratedAt` / `freshnessReason` whenever present (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts`). The shared project contract also requires `lastHydratedResolvedRef` and `lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef` on every source row (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts`), so unavailable rows returned from real GET surfaces can still expose prior hydration details. The only new TC-6.2a proof is a synthetic UI-envelope test (`tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts`), which means the route/read path required by the story’s anti-shim rule is not actually proving redaction.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:635:      - \"Real project/process read APIs still rely on client-side hiding for unavailable-source redaction; the runtime payloads can carry prior hydration metadata for degraded rows.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:672:      {\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’m tracing the unavailable-source redaction path first so we can fix the serialization bug at the source, then I’ll wire route-level tests that prove the real read behavior and run the story-focused checks.\"}}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:762:- sequence=12; actionSequence=11; createdAt=2026-05-04T23:20:55.317Z; note=\"After quick-fix returns, run verification again focused on SV-06-01, TC-6.2a real read-path redaction, and story gate evidence before considering acceptance.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:888:    selfNote: \"After quick-fix returns, run verification again focused on SV-06-01, TC-6.2a real read-path redaction, and story gate evidence before considering acceptance.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:896:    note: \"After quick-fix returns, run verification again focused on SV-06-01, TC-6.2a real read-path redaction, and story gate evidence before considering acceptance.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/epic/002-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"534b94be-1b73-4c82-8992-de070b2fd652\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Current-source semantics are split across the epic: process materials, checkpointing, and rebuild planning use `resolveActiveProcessSourceAttachments`, but refresh targeting, project-shell refresh eligibility, and informed-work provenance still trust raw durable `currentMaterialRefs.sourceAttachmentIds`.\",\"Soft detach and process-scope shadowing therefore stop at the read-model boundary; some runtime paths still treat detached or shadowed rows as current after the UI has hidden or replaced them.\",\"The provenance API shape is ahead of the runtime: degraded visibility modes such as `redacted` exist in the contract and renderer, but not in any real production write path.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design makes active-source resolution the canonical rule for combining project-scoped and process-scoped sources, but `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor` and `DefaultSourceProvenanceService.recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources` bypass that policy and reconstruct their own source sets from raw refs.\",\"Soft detach is implemented durably (`detachedAt`, `detachedByUserId`) and respected by the main readers, but older raw-ref consumers can still pull detached rows back into refresh/recovery decisions.\",\"The published provenance contract advertises `currentAttachmentVisibility: redacted`, but the implementation has no architecture path that detects revoked enrichment access and materializes that state.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Epic gate passed: `corepack pnpm run verify-all` completed successfully on May 4, 2026. The `test:e2e` leg is still scaffold-only and prints `SKIP: test:e2e scaffolded in Story 0; no executable suite yet`.\",\"Automated coverage exercises attach/update/detach flows, branch-drift freshness, refresh settled/pending/failed responses, and ready/degraded provenance rendering.\",\"Coverage does not exercise shadowed-source refresh/recovery or informed-work provenance recording when both project- and process-scoped ids remain durably current; the only explicit shadowing check I found is contract/fixture-level (`tests/service/server/source-management-contracts.test.ts:41-62`), and the redacted provenance path is only test-seeded (`tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:1099-1167`).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Source refresh is wired to real GitHub/provider seams, but its working-set planner still rehydrates from raw durable source ids, so detached or shadowed rows can flow back into a real provider hydration.\",\"The `redacted` provenance visibility branch is currently contract-only: no production writer emits `access_revoked` or any other degraded provenance row for that path.\",\"Process execution still uses the shared Epic 3 placeholder script payload, so the provenance hooks run against a non-domain-specific execution path even though persistence and checkpoint integrations are real.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-06-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Refresh planning bypasses active-source resolution and can rehydrate detached or shadowed-out sources\",\"evidence\":\"`RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.refreshRecoverableSource()` resolves target ownership and builds the hydration plan from raw `currentMaterialRefs.sourceAttachmentIds` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts:92-159,215-240`) instead of the active-source resolver used by checkpointing and rebuild planning (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts:13-62`, `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:751-760,1269-1289`). Because process-scoped attach only appends the new id and detach only stamps `detachedAt` (`convex/sourceAttachments.ts:148-158,279-317`), refreshing one source can still target or hydrate rows that the canonical current-source model has already shadowed or detached. The same raw ids also drive `projectRefreshTargetCount` in the project shell (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts:36-66`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-3.3\",\"AC-5.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-06-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Informed-work provenance ignores shadowing and can record duplicate or wrong-scope source relationships\",\"evidence\":\"`recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources()` iterates `currentMaterialRefs.sourceAttachmentIds` directly and records every distinct id (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:36-75`). When a process-scoped attachment shadows a project-scoped sibling, both ids remain durably current because process attach only appends the new id (`convex/sourceAttachments.ts:148-158`), while the canonical current-source read model collapses them via `resolveActiveProcessSourceAttachments()` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts:13-62`). `buildSourceProvenanceEntry()` then exposes whichever recorded row was stored, including its scope/access/hydration (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:174-230`), so provenance can claim both attachments informed the run or attribute informed work to the shadowed project-scoped row that the process materials view no longer shows.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-06-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"The shipped runtime cannot produce the required redacted provenance state\",\"evidence\":\"The response contract and renderer support `currentAttachmentVisibility: 'redacted'` / `degradationReason: 'access_revoked'` (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/source-management.ts:97-152`, `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:202-228`), but the only production write path always persists provenance as `entryStatus: 'ready'` with `degradationReason: null` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:153-171`). The only exercised redacted path is test-seeded data (`tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:1099-1167`). No non-test code writes `access_revoked` or any other degraded provenance row.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/source-management.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-06-004\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Source provenance is wired to the shared placeholder execution payload\",\"evidence\":\"Process execution still defaults to `buildDefaultScriptPayload()` and its embedded placeholder script (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:9-104`). The epic's real provenance hooks run off that execution/checkpoint path (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:549-568,830-839`), so informed-work and code-update provenance are currently attached to placeholder execution behavior until process-type-specific orchestration lands.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"AGENTS.md requires `docs/onboarding/current-state-index.md` and related onboarding docs, but `docs/onboarding/` is absent from this checkout, so I had to review directly from the epic spec pack and code.\",\"The fix shape for provenance `access_revoked` is still unsettled: the codebase needs either a real write-time producer or a read-time derivation rule for redacted entries.\",\"There is still no browser-level executable e2e proof for the full attach -> refresh -> provenance journey because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"227f9ac8-5f68-4295-a38a-83e3a6bb80e8\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Process-scoped shadowing is only enforced in read/checkpoint paths; provenance recording and runtime refresh still consume raw current source refs, so the same process can show one canonical source in materials while recording or hydrating a different set underneath.\",\"The source-management stack treats project source listings as exhaustive, but the underlying Convex query truncates them to 200 rows. Older attached/current sources can silently disappear from provenance and hydration flows even though their durable rows still exist.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Tech Design Q6/Q7 says process-scoped rows shadow project-scoped rows for process current-source behavior, but `DefaultSourceProvenanceService` and `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor` bypass `resolveActiveProcessSourceAttachments` and therefore drift from the declared resolver contract.\",\"The durable/read contract for attached sources is not pagination-safe: `convex/sourceAttachments.ts` caps project source listings at 200, while refresh/provenance builders assume that list is the full authoritative set.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` passed on May 4, 2026.\",\"`corepack pnpm run verify-all` passed on May 4, 2026, but its final `test:e2e` step is still scaffold-only and exits with a SKIP message rather than exercising an executable browser suite.\",\"The passing automated coverage does not exercise shadowed-source provenance, shadowed-source refresh, or >200-source project listings, which is why the defects below were not caught by the gate.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Runtime refresh is wired to real provider adapters, but the shadowed-source path can hydrate the wrong working set because `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor` rebuilds refresh plans from raw material refs instead of the canonical active-source resolver.\",\"Informed-work provenance still depends on the default Epic 3 execution placeholder payload, so part of this epic's production provenance path still runs through a non-domain-specific execution script.\",\"Redacted provenance is representable in contracts/tests, but runtime code does not currently produce `access_revoked` provenance entries; existing coverage seeds that degraded state directly.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-E6-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Shadowed project-scoped sources are still recorded as canonical process provenance\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultSourceProvenanceService.recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources` iterates raw `currentMaterialRefs.sourceAttachmentIds` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:36-74`). Process-scoped attaches append their id without removing the shared project id (`convex/sourceAttachments.ts:442-457`), while shadowing is only defined in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts:13-63`. Reproduced with an in-memory store: one project-scoped plus one process-scoped `acme/repo@main` produced 2 `informed_work` provenance rows instead of the single visible process-scoped source.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-4.2\",\"AC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-E6-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Refresh can target a shadowed project source and hydrate the wrong working set\",\"evidence\":\"`RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId` and `refreshRecoverableSource` use raw `currentMaterialRefs.sourceAttachmentIds` and then feed them straight into `planHydrationWorkingSet` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts:92-159,223-320`). That bypasses the active-source resolver that the main environment hydration path uses (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:1275-1289`). Reproduced with an in-memory store: refreshing a project-scoped source shadowed by a process-scoped sibling settled successfully and the adapter received both source ids in the hydration plan.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"AC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-E6-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Project source listings are hard-capped at 200 rows, breaking older current-source/runtime paths\",\"evidence\":\"`convex/sourceAttachments.ts:42-53` returns project source summaries with `.take(200)`. `DefaultSourceProvenanceService` and `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.buildAdapterHydrationPlan` both treat `listProjectSourceAttachments` as exhaustive (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:41-54,87-95`; `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts:260-318`). Reproduced by simulating the real capped store behavior: when a process current ref pointed at the 205th attachment, provenance recording created 0 rows; the refresh path would hit `HydrationPlan references sourceAttachmentId ... not in the project's source listing.`\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-3.3\",\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-E6-N001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Informed-work provenance still runs through the default execution placeholder\",\"evidence\":\"`ScriptExecutionService` still defaults every execution to `buildDefaultScriptPayload`, whose source is explicitly labeled `liminal-build default execution placeholder` and writes the `shared Epic 3 placeholder execution payload` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:9-24,76-104`). That does not break Epic 6 storage directly, but the production provenance signal for `informed_work` is still tied to a placeholder execution lane.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-E6-N002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Redacted provenance is test-seeded rather than runtime-produced\",\"evidence\":\"`createProvenanceRecord` always persists `entryStatus: 'ready'` with `degradationReason: null` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:153-171`), and no runtime path writes `access_revoked`. `buildSourceProvenanceEntry` can emit `currentAttachmentVisibility: 'redacted'` only when a stored degraded record already carries that reason (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:174-230`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"`docs/onboarding/current-state-index.md`, `current-state-tech-design.md`, and `current-state-code-map.md` are referenced by `AGENTS.md` but are absent in this worktree, so the review baseline had to come from the epic artifacts and code directly.\",\"`verify-all` passed, but `test:e2e` is still scaffold-only, so there is no executable end-to-end coverage for the epic's shadowing/provenance/refresh interactions.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/epic/002-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T00:02:27.732Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T00:09:10.752Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:19:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"run-quick-fix\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Latest verification outcome is revise with three blocking findings. The smallest safe next action is a bounded fix pass targeting the open Story 4 findings: mixed-success checkpoint provenance recording, redacted provenance visibility, and the format gate failure.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"findingRefs\\\":[\\\"story4-received-code-update-partial-success\\\",\\\"story4-redacted-visibility-unimplemented\\\",\\\"story4-story-gate-format-failure\\\"],\\\"remediationGoal\\\":\\\"Fix Story 4 blocking findings by recording received_code_update provenance for successful writable checkpoint targets even when sibling targets fail, implementing the required redacted currentAttachmentVisibility path with API coverage, and resolving the client test formatting failure without broad unrelated changes.\\\"},\\\"selfNote\\\":\\\"After quick-fix, re-run verification focused on the three open findings plus story gate: mixed-success checkpoint received_code_update provenance, redacted visibility, and format/green-verify.\\\"}\"}}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:23:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"run-verify\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The latest bounded child operation is a quick-fix that reports ready-for-verification after addressing the three open blocking findings from verifier result 007. Acceptance is not allowed until a verifier pass confirms the fixes and the story gate outcome, so the smallest safe next action is focused verification against that quick-fix artifact.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"artifactRefs\\\":[\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/quick-fix/003-quick-fix.json\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/007-verify.json\\\"],\\\"verifierContinuationRef\\\":\\\"storyVerifier\\\",\\\"responseArtifactRef\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/quick-fix/003-quick-fix.json\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Verify that quick-fix 003 resolves the prior open findings: mixed-success checkpoint received_code_update provenance recording, redacted provenance visibility, and the Story 4 format/green-verify gate failure. Confirm no new regressions in Story 4 requirements AC-4.1 through AC-4.4 and rerun the configured story gate corepack pnpm run green-verify.\\\"}}\"}}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:43:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"accept-story\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Latest verifier result is pass, all Story 4 mapped requirements are verified, no open findings remain, and the configured story gate `corepack pnpm run green-verify` passed. Story-lead can recommend acceptance while leaving final acceptance/receipts/commit authority to impl-lead.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Story 4 provenance and canonical source visibility is ready for impl-lead acceptance review. Implementation records and renders `informed_work` and `received_code_update` provenance, excludes read-only sources from write-target provenance, preserves healthy entries when another entry degrades, falls back to durable identity for degraded entries, handles redacted visibility, and no longer masks provenance fetch failures as true empty state.\\\",\\\"acceptanceCheckRefs\\\":[\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/013-verify.json\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/003-implementor.json\\\"],\\\"acceptanceChecks\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Story requirements coverage\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier 013 reports verified coverage for TC-4.1a, TC-4.1b, TC-4.2a, TC-4.3a, TC-4.4a, TC-4.4b, S4-NT-1, and S4-NT-2.\\\",\\\"Verifier 013 reports no unverified requirements and no open findings.\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"All story-local acceptance criteria and planned Story 4 tests are covered by the final verifier result.\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Story gate\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier 013 reports `corepack pnpm run green-verify` passed through format, lint, typecheck, build, `test:convex`, `test:service`, `test:client`, `test:packages`, and guard.\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"The configured story gate passed after the final quick-fix.\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Prior blockers resolved\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"SV-04-001 was resolved by preventing provenance fetch failures from rendering as true empty provenance.\\\",\\\"story4-received-code-update-partial-success was resolved by recording successful write-target provenance before mixed checkpoint failure handling.\\\",\\\"story4-redacted-visibility-unimplemented was resolved by emitting redacted visibility for access-revoked current attachment context.\\\",\\\"story4-story-gate-format-failure and story4-story-gate-typecheck-failure were resolved before verifier 013 passed.\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"All previously blocking verifier findings have durable resolution evidence in 