ce-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-22-Output configuration: Config A. Epic 6 gets this `tech-design.md` and a separate\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-23-`test-plan.md`. The work crosses client, Fastify, Convex, environment, and\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:24:GitHub boundaries, but the source-management slice is still coherent enough to\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-25-keep implementation depth in one index document.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-26-\\n--\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-33-| Issue | Spec Location | Resolution | Status |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-34-|-------|---------------|------------|--------|\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:35:| Source identity needs both operational URL and canonical GitHub identity | Data Contracts, AC-1.3, AC-4.x | Design stores `repositoryUrl` for clone/write operations and `repositoryFullName` for uniqueness/provenance. `repositoryFullName` is derived server-side when omitted. | Resolved - clarified |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:36:| Refresh cannot always settle synchronously | AC-3.3, Refresh Response | Design returns `refreshStatus: settled | pending | failed`, with pending as operation metadata rather than a fifth hydration state. | Resolved - clarified |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:37:| Process-scoped shadowing needs exact read rule | Tech Design Question 7 | Design defines an active-source resolver that combines project-scoped and process-scoped attachments, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, and excludes detached rows. | Resolved |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-38-| Detach representation needs exact storage shape | Tech Design Question 8 | Design adds soft-detach fields (`detachedAt`, `detachedByUserId`) and active-list filters. | Resolved |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-39-| Source provenance storage is deferred by epic | AC-4.x | Design introduces durable `sourceProvenance` records with copied immutable source identity. | Resolved |\\n--\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-50-| 2 | What exact durable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-51-| 3 | What exact conflict rule applies for same repository/target ref across related contexts? | Duplicate key is active `projectId + processId + repositoryFullName + targetRef`. Same identity/ref may exist once at project scope and once at process scope. Process-scoped rows shadow project-scoped rows only for that process's current-source read. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:52:| 4 | What exact refresh/freshness policy maps to the four source states? | The canonical states remain `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, and `unavailable`. Target-ref changes make hydrated rows stale. Refresh returns settled/pending/failed operation metadata; pending is not a fifth hydration state. Branch freshness is checked when the surface reads or refresh is requested, not by background polling. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-53-| 5 | What provenance surface shows informed-work and received-code-update relationships? | Add a process provenance endpoint and client section that reads durable `sourceProvenance` entries. Entries are `informed_work` or `received_code_update`, copy repository identity, and enrich current attachment context independently when available. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-54-| 6 | How should shell/process surfaces stay coherent across project and process scope? | Keep project shell source summaries for project-wide management. Process work surfaces show current sources after active-source resolution, including process-scoped shadowing and applicable project-scoped rows. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:55:| 7 | What exact current-source read algorithm combines scopes and degrades boundedly? | `resolveActiveProcessSources` excludes detached rows, starts from current material refs, pulls in process-scoped siblings when they shadow an active project-scoped source, partitions by scope, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, sorts by `updatedAt`, and preserves per-row degraded metadata. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-56-| 8 | What soft-detach representation preserves identity and provenance? | Add `detachedAt` and `detachedByUserId` to source attachments. Active listings filter detached rows, but provenance entries remain durable because they copy identity and may retain nullable `sourceAttachmentId`. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-57-\\n--\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-67-\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-68-The missing layer is user- and process-facing source management. A user needs to\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:69:attach a GitHub repository to a project or to one process, classify why it is\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-70-attached, understand whether it can receive writes, refresh stale or missing\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-71-working copies, detach it from current use without erasing history, and later\\n--\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-73-cannot be implicit side effects of environment hydration.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-74-\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:75:The core architecture shapes the design. GitHub remains code truth. The\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-76-sandboxed filesystem is only a disposable working copy. Fastify is the source\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-77-management control plane: it validates repository identity, enforces project and\\n--\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-108-    STORE[PlatformStore]\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-109-    X[(Convex)]\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:110:    GH[GitHub]\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/te