ent services rather than assuming a full source-management implementation already exists |\\n--\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-152-| Decision | Rationale | Consequence |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-153-|----------|-----------|-------------|\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:154:| Keep `repositoryUrl` and add `repositoryFullName` | `repositoryUrl` is operational clone/write input; `owner/name` is stable GitHub identity for uniqueness and provenance | Create accepts URL-first requests and may derive full name; persisted summaries return both |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-155-| Source-management routes live in Fastify | Architecture says Fastify owns orchestration, auth, integrations, and source policy | Convex functions remain trusted persistence operations, not public app API |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-156-| Soft detach rather than hard delete | Prior provenance and historical source identity must remain visible after detach | Active source reads filter detached rows; provenance can still resolve copied identity |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:157:| Refresh may be pending | Repo fetch/hydration work can exceed a short request | Pending state is operation metadata, not a fifth canonical hydration state |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-158-| Process-scoped attach updates current process source refs immediately | The epic says a process-scoped attachment belongs to one process as current source state and becomes visible immediately | `attachProcessSource` persists the source row and adds its id to that process's current source refs in the same orchestration path |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:159:| Process scope shadows project scope only in current-source reads | Same repo can be useful both project-wide and process-specific | Durable rows can coexist; resolver picks process-scoped row for that process when identity/ref collide |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-160-| Read-write attachments require branch-like target refs | Durable code updates need a writable moving ref rather than an immutable commit/tag | `read_write` attachments reject tag/commit target refs; `read_only` attachments may use branch/tag/commit |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-161-| Provenance records copy immutable identity | Detach or access loss must not erase process history | Provenance stores `repositoryFullName`, `repositoryUrl`, `targetRef`, relationship kind, and optional attachment id |\\n--\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-185-├── source-management.service.ts                 # NEW: orchestration, validation, conflict/shadowing policy\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-186-├── source-identity.service.ts                   # NEW: URL parsing, canonical full-name derivation, target-ref normalization\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:187:├── github-repository-resolver.ts                # NEW: GitHub access/ref validation boundary\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-188-├── source-refresh.service.ts                    # NEW: refresh request handling and pending/settled result shaping\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-m