{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_101","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"AC-4 provenance behavior is inconsistent across the epic: `informed_work` is over-attributed to every current source, while `received_code_update` is unreachable on the default runtime path.\",\"Detach/read/hydration stories are not fully aligned: detached attachments disappear from current-source views, but durable working-set state can still carry them forward into environment fingerprints.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The runtime contract does not expose source-use signals, even though the tech design assigns source-use/code-update signaling to the tool runtime, so the provenance layer cannot distinguish \\\"attached\\\" from \\\"actually used.\\\"\",\"Working-set truth is split across current material refs, active-source resolution, and persisted environment fingerprints; detach only updates the attachment row, which creates cross-story drift.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Focused Epic 6 suites pass when run directly: 78 server/convex tests and 20 client tests passed.\",\"Attach/update/refresh/detach surfaces are broadly implemented, but the provenance guarantees still rely on test seams or inferred state instead of the real production default path.\",\"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both fail before the epic suites run because Biome rejects the nested root configuration at `packages/lbuild-impl/biome.json`.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The default runtime still uses the placeholder execution payload, so the production path never emits code checkpoint candidates and cannot generate `received_code_update` provenance.\",\"`createApp` still allows a story0/`NullPlatformStore` fallback in production after only a warning, leaving a non-real control-plane path available under misconfiguration.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EF-01\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Informed-work provenance records every current source, not the sources actually used\",\"evidence\":\"`ExecutionResult` has no source-use field (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:125-131`). After every run, `ProcessEnvironmentService` unconditionally calls `recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:565-568`), and `DefaultSourceProvenanceService` then writes one `informed_work` row per active current source (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:48-76`). A run can therefore claim provenance for repositories the execution never touched.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EF-02\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"The default production execution path cannot produce received_code_update provenance\",\"evidence\":\"`createApp` wires `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:266-267`). That service still ships the explicit placeholder payload (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:9-68`), and the payload emits `codeCheckpointCandidates: []`. Normal runtime executions therefore cannot reach the code-write/provenance lane needed for `received_code_update` entries.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.2\",\"AC-4.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EF-03\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Detach does not fully remove a source from durable working-set state\",\"evidence\":\"`detachSourceAttachment` only stamps `detachedAt` on the source row (`convex/sourceAttachments.ts:279-317`). The persisted environment fingerprint still hashes every `currentSourceAttachmentId` without filtering detached rows (`convex/processEnvironmentStates.ts:245-290`), and `setProcessHydrationPlan` recomputes that fingerprint from the stale refs instead of from the filtered plan (`convex/processEnvironmentStates.ts:563-620`). Start/resume build hydration plans from `resolveActiveProcessSourceAttachments` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-start.service.ts:57-78`), so later hydrations can exclude a detached source while the stored fingerprint still claims it is part of the working set.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\",\"convex/processEnvironmentStates.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-start.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-resume.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EF-04\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production bootstrap still tolerates the story0/NullPlatformStore fallback\",\"evidence\":\"`createApp` defaults to `story0PlaceholderEnv` and swaps in `NullPlatformStore` whenever `hasLiveConvexConfig` is false (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:171-185`; `apps/platform/server/config.ts:48-72`), then only logs a warning in production (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:205-208`). `NullPlatformStore` still returns synthetic process/source objects and placeholder repository identity in its source-management methods (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:912-1247`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/config.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` fails at `format:check` because Biome reports a nested root configuration in `packages/lbuild-impl/biome.json`.\",\"`corepack pnpm run verify-all` fails for the same reason before integration/e2e phases start.\"],\"gateResult\":\"fail\"}"}}
